# Player guide

Build a race, choose your opponents, and start exploring the galaxy.
These guides explain the choices you make in craig-stars and include interactive examples you can try before creating a game.

## Start playing

[Create a game](/docs/games/create) walks through choosing a race, galaxy settings, player slots, AI difficulty, and victory conditions. Start with a single-player game or host a game for other people.

The [game creation example](/docs/games/create#try-it) uses the same controls as the real game. Change settings, add players, and preview your setup without signing in or saving anything.

## Connect an assistant

[MCP setup](/docs/mcp) explains how to connect an assistant to your games with Claude, Codex, or another MCP client.
